{"name":"Attica","hex":"#a1bca9","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Attica","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A periphery where Athens, the capital of Greece, is located.","A peninsula southeast of Athens, Greece."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Attica"}],"entries":[{"title":"Attica","blocks":[{"text":"Attica, or the Attic Peninsula, is a historical region that encompasses the entire Athens metropolitan area, which consists of the city of Athens, the capital of Greece and the core city of the metropolitan area, as well as its surrounding suburban cities and towns. It is a peninsula projecting into the Aegean Sea, bordering on Boeotia to the north and Megaris to the west. The mines of Laurion were an important mining region located at Lavrio, on the southern tip of the peninsula."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Attica_06-13_Hills_of_Hymettus_10_view.jpg/330px-Attica_06-13_Hills_of_Hymettus_10_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Attica","wikidata":"Q122443"},{"title":"Attica (region)","blocks":[{"text":"Attica is an administrative region of Greece that encompasses the entire Athens metropolitan area, the core city of which is the country's capital and largest city, Athens. The region is coextensive with the former Attica Prefecture of Central Greece and covers a greater area than the historical region of Attica."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Griechisches_Parlament_nachts_%28Zuschnitt%29.jpg/330px-Griechisches_Parlament_nachts_%28Zuschnitt%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Attica_(region)","wikidata":"Q758056"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Aliki_Anavyssou.JPG/500px-Aliki_Anavyssou.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&